/-!
# The fixed Weyl group of a root-pairing automorphism

Given an automorphism `σ` of a root pairing `P`, the **fixed Weyl group**
`RootPairing.fixedWeylGroup P σ` is the subgroup `W^σ` of Weyl-group elements commuting with `σ`
inside `P.Aut` — equivalently, the fixed points of conjugation `σ.weylGroupEquiv` on `P.weylGroup`,
or, when `σ` stabilizes a base `b`, of the semidirect-product conjugation action `b.conjWeylGroup`.

Every element of `W^σ` preserves the fixed weight submodule `LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap`,
giving `W^σ` a canonical `R`-linear action on `E^σ`. When `σ` stabilizes a base `b` of a finite
reduced crystallographic root pairing over a characteristic-zero domain, this restricted action is
faithful and, under pairwise orthogonality of each `σ`-orbit of simple roots, is generated by the
products of simple reflections over the simple-root orbits (Stembridge, Claim 3):

1. **Faithfulness on `E^σ`.** Because `σ` permutes the positive roots of `b`, twice the Weyl vector
   `2ρ` lies in `E^σ`. Any Weyl-group element fixing `E^σ` pointwise fixes `2ρ` and is therefore
   the identity (`TauCeti.eq_one_of_smul_twoWeylVector_eq`), with no order on the coefficient ring
   or spanning hypothesis needed. Over a linearly ordered ring, `2ρ` also witnesses that the open
   dominant chamber meets `E^σ`.
2. **Generation by simple-orbit reflection products.** For any `σ`-orbit `O = P.orbitIndices σ i`
   whose members pair to `0` away from the diagonal, `σ`-invariance makes `O` pairwise orthogonal,
   so the unordered product `s_O = ∏_{j ∈ O} sⱼ` in `W` is well defined, commutes with `σ`, and acts
   on `x ∈ E^σ` as the reflection `x ↦ x - ⟨x, αᵢ^∨⟩ (∑_{j ∈ O} αⱼ)`. When `σ` stabilizes `b` and
   every simple-root orbit has this property, the inversion set of any `w ∈ W^σ` is `σ`-invariant:
   if `w ≠ 1`, some simple root `αᵢ` is an inversion of `w`, hence its entire `σ`-orbit `O` lies in
   `inversions P b w`, right multiplication by `s_O` stays in `W^σ` while lowering the inversion
   count by `#O`, and strong induction expresses `w` as a product of the generators `s_O`.

## Main definitions

* `RootPairing.fixedWeylGroup`: the subgroup `W^σ ≤ P.weylGroup` of Weyl-group elements commuting
  with `σ : P.Aut`.
* `RootPairing.Equiv.fixedWeylGroupMulEquiv`: transport `P.fixedWeylGroup σ ≃* Q.fixedWeylGroup τ`
  along an equivalence `e : P.Equiv Q` satisfying `e.autCongr σ = τ`.
* `DistribMulAction (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap)` and the companion
  `SMulCommClass` instance: the restricted `R`-linear action of `W^σ` on `E^σ`.

## Main results

* `RootPairing.mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff`, `RootPairing.mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_weylGroupEquiv`,
  `RootPairing.Base.mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_conjWeylGroup`, and
  `RootPairing.mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_forall_weightMap_smul`: equivalent characterizations of `W^σ`
  via commutation in `P.Aut`, conjugation on `W`, and equivariance on weights (and on root indices
  when the roots span, `RootPairing.mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_commute_weylGroupToPerm`).
* `RootPairing.Base.twoWeylVector_mem_fixedSubmodule` and
  `RootPairing.Base.openDominantChamber_inter_fixedSubmodule_nonempty`: `2ρ` is fixed by every based
  automorphism and witnesses that the open dominant chamber meets `E^σ`.
* `RootPairing.Base.eq_one_of_forall_mem_fixedSubmodule_smul_eq`,
  `RootPairing.Base.fixingSubgroup_fixedSubmodule_eq_bot`,
  `RootPairing.Base.faithfulSMul_fixedWeylGroup_fixedSubmodule`, and
  `RootPairing.Base.toModuleAut_fixedWeylGroup_injective`: the Weyl group has trivial pointwise
  stabilizer on `E^σ`, so `W^σ` acts faithfully on `E^σ`.
* `RootPairing.Base.indexEquiv_mem_inversions_iff` and
  `RootPairing.Base.orbitIndices_subset_inversions`: for `σ ∈ b.basedAut` and `w ∈ W^σ`, the
  inversion set `inversions P b w` is a union of `σ`-orbits.
* `RootPairing.pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices_iff`,
  `RootPairing.noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_mem_fixedWeylGroup`, and
  `RootPairing.noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_smul_of_mem_fixedSubmodule`: an orbit reflection
  product lies in `W^σ` and acts on `E^σ` by `x ↦ x - ⟨x, αᵢ^∨⟩ • P.orbitSum σ i`.
* `RootPairing.Base.fixedWeylGroup_eq_closure`,
  `RootPairing.Base.top_eq_closure_fixedWeylGroup`, and
  `RootPairing.Base.range_toModuleAut_fixedWeylGroup`: when `σ ∈ b.basedAut` has orthogonal
  simple-root orbits, the simple-orbit reflection products generate `W^σ` and its linear image in
  `E^σ ≃ₗ[R] E^σ`.

## References

* J. R. Stembridge, *Folding by automorphisms*, note of 20 August 2008, Claim 3.
* G. Lusztig, *Introduction to Quantum Groups*, Progress in Mathematics 110, Part II, §14.1.
* N. Bourbaki, *Lie Groups and Lie Algebras, Chapters 4--6*, Ch. VI, §1.
-/

public section

open Finset Function Set TauCeti

namespace RootPairing

universe u v w x

variable {ι : Type u} {R : Type v} {M : Type w} {N : Type x}
  [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N]

/-! ### The fixed Weyl group and its characterizations -/

/-- The **fixed Weyl group** `W^σ` of an automorphism `σ` of a root pairing `P`: the subgroup of
`P.weylGroup` consisting of elements that commute with `σ` in `P.Aut`. -/
noncomputable def fixedWeylGroup (P : RootPairing ι R M N) (σ : P.Aut) : Subgroup P.weylGroup :=
  (Subgroup.centralizer ({σ} : Set P.Aut)).comap P.weylGroup.subtype

theorem fixedWeylGroup_def (P : RootPairing ι R M N) (σ : P.Aut) :
    P.fixedWeylGroup σ = (Subgroup.centralizer ({σ} : Set P.Aut)).comap P.weylGroup.subtype :=
  (rfl)

variable {P : RootPairing ι R M N} {σ : P.Aut} {w : P.weylGroup}

/-- A Weyl-group element lies in `P.fixedWeylGroup σ` precisely when it commutes with `σ` in
`P.Aut`.

Stated with `Commute` on the right-hand side rather than `(w : P.Aut) * σ = σ * (w : P.Aut)`
because `RootPairing.Equiv.mul_eq_comp` rewrites products in `P.Aut` under `simp`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ ↔ Commute (w : P.Aut) σ := by
  rw [fixedWeylGroup, Subgroup.mem_comap, Subgroup.coe_subtype,
    Subgroup.mem_centralizer_singleton_iff, commute_iff_eq]

theorem mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_mul_eq :
    w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ ↔ (w : P.Aut) * σ = σ * (w : P.Aut) := by
  rw [mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff, commute_iff_eq]

theorem mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_conj_eq :
    w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ ↔ σ * (w : P.Aut) * σ⁻¹ = (w : P.Aut) := by
  rw [mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_mul_eq, mul_inv_eq_iff_eq_mul, eq_comm]

/-- A Weyl-group element lies in `P.fixedWeylGroup σ` precisely when conjugation by `σ` fixes it in
`P.weylGroup`. -/
theorem mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_weylGroupEquiv :
    w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ ↔ σ.weylGroupEquiv w = w := by
  have hcoe : (σ.weylGroupEquiv w : P.Aut) = σ * (w : P.Aut) * σ⁻¹ := by
    rw [Equiv.coe_weylGroupEquiv, Equiv.autCongr_apply, mul_assoc]
    rfl
  rw [← Subtype.coe_inj, hcoe, mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_conj_eq]

/-- For a based automorphism `δ : b.basedAut`, the fixed Weyl group is the fixed-point subgroup of
the semidirect-product conjugation action `b.conjWeylGroup δ`. -/
theorem Base.mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_conjWeylGroup {b : P.Base} {δ : b.basedAut} :
    w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup (δ : P.Aut) ↔ b.conjWeylGroup δ w = w := by
  rw [← Subtype.coe_inj, b.coe_conjWeylGroup_apply, mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_conj_eq]

/-- A Weyl-group element lies in `P.fixedWeylGroup σ` precisely when its action on weights commutes
with `σ.weightMap`. -/
theorem mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_forall_weightMap_smul :
    w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ ↔ ∀ x : M, σ.weightMap (w • x) = w • σ.weightMap x := by
  rw [mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_mul_eq, ← (Equiv.weightHom_injective P).eq_iff, map_mul, map_mul,
    LinearEquiv.ext_iff]
  simp only [Equiv.weightHom_apply, mul_apply_eq_comp, Equiv.weightEquiv_apply,
    Subgroup.smul_def, eq_comm]
  rfl

/-- Weight-space equivariance in action notation characterizing membership in
`P.fixedWeylGroup σ`. -/
theorem mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_forall_smul :
    w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ ↔ ∀ x : M, σ • w • x = w • σ • x :=
  mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_forall_weightMap_smul

theorem weightMap_smul_of_mem_fixedWeylGroup (hw : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ) (x : M) :
    σ.weightMap (w • x) = w • σ.weightMap x :=
  mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_forall_weightMap_smul.mp hw x

theorem commute_weylGroupToPerm_of_mem_fixedWeylGroup (hw : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ) :
    Commute (P.weylGroupToPerm w) σ.indexEquiv :=
  (mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff.mp hw).map (Equiv.indexHom P)

theorem indexEquiv_weylGroupToPerm_of_mem_fixedWeylGroup (hw : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ) (i : ι) :
    σ.indexEquiv (P.weylGroupToPerm w i) = P.weylGroupToPerm w (σ.indexEquiv i) := by
  have h := (commute_weylGroupToPerm_of_mem_fixedWeylGroup hw).symm.eq
  exact congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe h) i

/-- When the roots span the weight space, `w` lies in `P.fixedWeylGroup σ` precisely when its root
index permutation commutes with `σ.indexEquiv`. -/
theorem mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_commute_weylGroupToPerm_of_span_eq_top
    (hspan : Submodule.span R (range P.root) = ⊤) :
    w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ ↔ Commute (P.weylGroupToPerm w) σ.indexEquiv := by
  rw [mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff, commute_iff_eq, commute_iff_eq,
    ← (Equiv.indexHom_injective_of_span_eq_top P hspan).eq_iff, map_mul, map_mul]
  rfl

/-- For a root system, `w` lies in `P.fixedWeylGroup σ` precisely when its root index permutation
commutes with `σ.indexEquiv`. -/
theorem mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_commute_weylGroupToPerm [P.IsRootSystem] :
    w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ ↔ Commute (P.weylGroupToPerm w) σ.indexEquiv :=
  mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_commute_weylGroupToPerm_of_span_eq_top
    (IsRootSystem.span_root_eq_top (P := P))

variable (P) in
/-- Every Weyl-group element commutes with the identity automorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem fixedWeylGroup_one : P.fixedWeylGroup 1 = ⊤ := by
  ext w
  simp [Commute.one_right]

variable (P) in
/-- An automorphism and its inverse have the same fixed Weyl group. -/
@[simp]
theorem fixedWeylGroup_inv (σ : P.Aut) : P.fixedWeylGroup σ⁻¹ = P.fixedWeylGroup σ := by
  ext w
  simp [Commute.inv_right_iff]

/-- Any Weyl-group element commuting with `σ` also commutes with every natural power `σ ^ n`. -/
theorem le_fixedWeylGroup_pow (n : ℕ) : P.fixedWeylGroup σ ≤ P.fixedWeylGroup (σ ^ n) :=
  fun _ hw ↦ mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff.mpr ((mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff.mp hw).pow_right n)

/-- Any Weyl-group element commuting with `σ` also commutes with every integer power `σ ^ n`. -/
theorem le_fixedWeylGroup_zpow (n : ℤ) : P.fixedWeylGroup σ ≤ P.fixedWeylGroup (σ ^ n) :=
  fun _ hw ↦ mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff.mpr ((mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff.mp hw).zpow_right n)

/-- Over an empty root index type, the fixed Weyl group is trivial. -/
noncomputable instance [IsEmpty ι] : Unique (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) where
  default := 1
  uniq := by
    rintro ⟨⟨g, hg⟩, hmem⟩
    have hg1 : g = 1 := by
      clear hmem
      induction hg using weylGroup.induction with
      | mem i => exact isEmptyElim i
      | one => rfl
      | mul _ _ _ _ h₁ h₂ => rw [h₁, h₂, mul_one]
    exact Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext hg1)

variable (P σ) in
/-- When the roots span a finite root pairing, the fixed Weyl group is finite. -/
theorem finite_fixedWeylGroup_of_span_eq_top [Finite ι]
    (hspan : Submodule.span R (range P.root) = ⊤) : Finite (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) :=
  have := P.finite_weylGroup_of_span_eq_top hspan
  Subtype.finite

variable (P σ) in
/-- The fixed Weyl group of a finite root system is finite. -/
theorem finite_fixedWeylGroup [Finite ι] [P.IsRootSystem] : Finite (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) :=
  have := P.finite_weylGroup
  Subtype.finite

/-! ### Transport along equivalences of root pairings -/

section Transport

variable {ι₂ M₂ N₂ : Type*} [AddCommGroup M₂] [Module R M₂] [AddCommGroup N₂] [Module R N₂]
  {Q : RootPairing ι₂ R M₂ N₂}

/-- An equivalence `e : P.Equiv Q` conjugating `σ` to `τ` maps `P.fixedWeylGroup σ` onto
`Q.fixedWeylGroup τ` under `e.weylGroupEquiv`. -/
theorem Equiv.map_fixedWeylGroup (e : P.Equiv Q) {σ : P.Aut} {τ : Q.Aut}
    (h : e.autCongr σ = τ) :
    (P.fixedWeylGroup σ).map e.weylGroupEquiv.toMonoidHom = Q.fixedWeylGroup τ := by
  subst h
  ext w
  rw [Subgroup.mem_map_equiv, mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff, mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff,
    Equiv.coe_weylGroupEquiv_symm, commute_iff_eq, commute_iff_eq,
    ← e.autCongr.injective.eq_iff, map_mul, map_mul, MulEquiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- **Transport of the fixed Weyl group along an equivalence of root pairings** intertwining the
two automorphisms. -/
noncomputable def Equiv.fixedWeylGroupMulEquiv (e : P.Equiv Q) {σ : P.Aut} {τ : Q.Aut}
    (h : e.autCongr σ = τ) : P.fixedWeylGroup σ ≃* Q.fixedWeylGroup τ :=
  (e.weylGroupEquiv.subgroupMap (P.fixedWeylGroup σ)).trans
    (MulEquiv.subgroupCongr (e.map_fixedWeylGroup h))

@[simp]
theorem Equiv.coe_fixedWeylGroupMulEquiv (e : P.Equiv Q) {σ : P.Aut} {τ : Q.Aut}
    (h : e.autCongr σ = τ) (w : P.fixedWeylGroup σ) :
    (e.fixedWeylGroupMulEquiv h w : Q.weylGroup) = e.weylGroupEquiv w :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem Equiv.coe_fixedWeylGroupMulEquiv_symm (e : P.Equiv Q) {σ : P.Aut} {τ : Q.Aut}
    (h : e.autCongr σ = τ) (w : Q.fixedWeylGroup τ) :
    ((e.fixedWeylGroupMulEquiv h).symm w : P.weylGroup) = e.weylGroupEquiv.symm w :=
  (rfl)

end Transport

/-! ### Restricted linear action on the fixed weight submodule -/

/-- Any Weyl-group element commuting with `σ` preserves the fixed submodule of `σ.weightMap`. -/
theorem smul_mem_fixedSubmodule (hw : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ)
    {x : M} (hx : x ∈ LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) :
    w • x ∈ LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap := by
  rw [LinearMap.mem_fixedSubmodule_iff] at hx ⊢
  rw [weightMap_smul_of_mem_fixedWeylGroup hw, hx]

noncomputable instance : SMul (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) where
  smul w x := ⟨(w : P.weylGroup) • (x : M), smul_mem_fixedSubmodule w.2 x.2⟩

@[simp]
theorem coe_smul_fixedSubmodule (w : P.fixedWeylGroup σ)
    (x : LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) :
    ((w • x : LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) : M) = (w : P.weylGroup) • (x : M) :=
  (rfl)

noncomputable instance : MulAction (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) where
  one_smul x := Subtype.ext (one_smul P.weylGroup (x : M))
  mul_smul v w x := Subtype.ext (mul_smul (v : P.weylGroup) (w : P.weylGroup) (x : M))

/-- The fixed Weyl group acts by additive automorphisms on the fixed weight submodule. Together
with `SMulCommClass (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) R (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap)`, Mathlib's
`DistribMulAction.toModuleAut` packages this action as a group homomorphism
`P.fixedWeylGroup σ →* (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap ≃ₗ[R]
LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap)`. -/
noncomputable instance :
    DistribMulAction (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) where
  smul_zero w := Subtype.ext (smul_zero (w : P.weylGroup))
  smul_add w x y := Subtype.ext (smul_add (w : P.weylGroup) (x : M) (y : M))

instance : SMulCommClass (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) R (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) where
  smul_comm w r x := Subtype.ext (smul_comm (w : P.weylGroup) r (x : M))

/-! ### Fixed Weyl vector and faithfulness on the fixed submodule -/

namespace Base

section WeylVector

variable [CharZero R] [Finite ι] {b : P.Base}

/-- A based automorphism fixes twice the Weyl vector `2ρ`. -/
theorem weightMap_twoWeylVector_of_mem_basedAut (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) :
    σ.weightMap (twoWeylVector P b) = twoWeylVector P b := by
  rw [σ.weightMap_twoWeylVector, map_eq_of_mem_basedAut hσ]

/-- Twice the Weyl vector `2ρ` lies in the fixed submodule of any based automorphism. -/
theorem twoWeylVector_mem_fixedSubmodule (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) :
    twoWeylVector P b ∈ LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap :=
  LinearMap.mem_fixedSubmodule_iff.mpr (weightMap_twoWeylVector_of_mem_basedAut hσ)

/-- When `2` is invertible, the Weyl vector `ρ` lies in the fixed submodule of any based
automorphism. -/
theorem weylVector_mem_fixedSubmodule [Invertible (2 : R)] (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) :
    weylVector P b ∈ LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap := by
  rw [LinearMap.mem_fixedSubmodule_iff, σ.weightMap_weylVector, map_eq_of_mem_basedAut hσ]

end WeylVector

section Ordered

variable [LinearOrder R] [IsStrictOrderedRing R] [Finite ι] [P.IsCrystallographic] [P.IsReduced]
  {b : P.Base}

/-- **The open dominant chamber meets the fixed submodule of any based automorphism.** -/
theorem openDominantChamber_inter_fixedSubmodule_nonempty (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) :
    (openDominantChamber P b ∩ (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap : Set M)).Nonempty :=
  ⟨twoWeylVector P b, twoWeylVector_mem_openDominantChamber P b,
    twoWeylVector_mem_fixedSubmodule hσ⟩

end Ordered

section Faithful

variable [Finite ι] [CharZero R] [IsDomain R] [P.IsCrystallographic] [P.IsReduced] {b : P.Base}

/-- **Any Weyl-group element fixing `E^σ` pointwise is the identity**, where `σ` is a based
automorphism, with no order on the coefficient ring or spanning hypothesis needed. -/
theorem eq_one_of_forall_mem_fixedSubmodule_smul_eq (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) {w : P.weylGroup}
    (hw : ∀ x ∈ LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap, w • x = x) : w = 1 :=
  eq_one_of_smul_twoWeylVector_eq P b (hw _ (twoWeylVector_mem_fixedSubmodule hσ))

/-- **The pointwise stabilizer in `P.weylGroup` of the fixed submodule of a based automorphism is
trivial.** -/
theorem fixingSubgroup_fixedSubmodule_eq_bot (b : P.Base) {σ : P.Aut} (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) :
    fixingSubgroup P.weylGroup (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap : Set M) = ⊥ := by
  ext w
  rw [mem_fixingSubgroup_iff, Subgroup.mem_bot]
  exact ⟨eq_one_of_forall_mem_fixedSubmodule_smul_eq hσ, fun h _ _ ↦ by rw [h, one_smul]⟩

/-- **The fixed Weyl group of a based automorphism acts faithfully on the fixed submodule.** -/
theorem faithfulSMul_fixedWeylGroup_fixedSubmodule (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) :
    FaithfulSMul (P.fixedWeylGroup σ) (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) :=
  ⟨fun {v w} h ↦ by
    have h1 : (v⁻¹ * w : P.fixedWeylGroup σ) = 1 := Subtype.ext <|
      eq_one_of_forall_mem_fixedSubmodule_smul_eq hσ fun x hx ↦ by
        have hx' := congrArg Subtype.val (h ⟨x, hx⟩)
        rw [coe_smul_fixedSubmodule, coe_smul_fixedSubmodule] at hx'
        rw [Subgroup.coe_mul, Subgroup.coe_inv, mul_smul, ← hx', inv_smul_smul]
    exact inv_mul_eq_one.mp h1⟩

/-- **The restricted linear representation of `W^σ` on `E^σ` is injective** (the injectivity half
of Stembridge, Claim 3). -/
theorem toModuleAut_fixedWeylGroup_injective (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) :
    Injective (DistribMulAction.toModuleAut R (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap)
      (S := P.fixedWeylGroup σ)) := by
  let _ := faithfulSMul_fixedWeylGroup_fixedSubmodule hσ
  intro v w h
  exact eq_of_smul_eq_smul fun x : LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap ↦
    congrArg (fun e : LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap ≃ₗ[R]
      LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap ↦ e x) h

/-- Two elements of `P.fixedWeylGroup σ` agreeing on `LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap` are
equal. -/
theorem fixedWeylGroup_ext (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) {v w : P.fixedWeylGroup σ}
    (h : ∀ x : LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap, v • x = w • x) : v = w := by
  let _ := faithfulSMul_fixedWeylGroup_fixedSubmodule hσ
  exact eq_of_smul_eq_smul h

end Faithful

/-! ### `σ`-invariance of inversion sets -/

section Inversions

variable [CharZero R] {b : P.Base}

/-- For a based automorphism `σ` and `w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ`, `σ.indexEquiv` preserves and
reflects membership in `inversions P b w`. -/
theorem indexEquiv_mem_inversions_iff (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) (hw : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ) (i : ι) :
    σ.indexEquiv i ∈ inversions P b w ↔ i ∈ inversions P b w := by
  have hsupp := mem_basedAut_iff_forall_mem_support.mp hσ
  rw [mem_inversions, mem_inversions, b.isPos_indexEquiv_iff hsupp,
    ← indexEquiv_weylGroupToPerm_of_mem_fixedWeylGroup hw, b.isPos_indexEquiv_iff hsupp]

/-- If `w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ` for a based automorphism `σ`, two indices in the same `σ`-orbit
simultaneously lie in or outside `inversions P b w`. -/
theorem mem_inversions_iff_of_mem_orbitIndices [Finite ι] (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut)
    (hw : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ) {i j : ι} (hj : j ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i) :
    j ∈ inversions P b w ↔ i ∈ inversions P b w := by
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := mem_orbitIndices_iff_exists_pow.mp hj
  clear hj
  induction k with
  | zero => simp
  | succ k ih => rw [pow_succ', Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, indexEquiv_mem_inversions_iff hσ hw, ih]

/-- **Every `σ`-orbit meeting `inversions P b w` is contained in `inversions P b w`**, when
`σ ∈ b.basedAut` and `w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ`. -/
theorem orbitIndices_subset_inversions [Finite ι] (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut)
    (hw : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ) {i : ι} (hi : i ∈ inversions P b w) :
    (P.orbitIndices σ i : Set ι) ⊆ inversions P b w :=
  fun _ hj ↦ (mem_inversions_iff_of_mem_orbitIndices hσ hw hj).mpr hi

end Inversions

/-- For a based automorphism `σ`, the `σ`-orbit of any simple root consists of simple roots. -/
theorem orbitIndices_subset_support [Finite ι] {b : P.Base} (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut)
    {i : ι} (hi : i ∈ b.support) : (P.orbitIndices σ i : Set ι) ⊆ b.support := by
  intro j hj
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := mem_orbitIndices_iff_exists_pow.mp hj
  have hpow : σ ^ k ∈ b.basedAut := pow_mem hσ k
  have hk : (σ.indexEquiv ^ k) i = (σ ^ k).indexEquiv i := by
    simpa using (congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe (map_pow (Equiv.indexHom P) σ k)) i).symm
  rw [Finset.mem_coe, hk]
  exact mem_basedAut_iff_forall_mem_support.mp hpow i hi

end Base

/-! ### Orbit reflection products and generation of the fixed Weyl group -/

section OrbitReflection

variable [Finite ι]

/-- **Vanishing of `P.pairing i j` away from `i` along a `σ`-orbit implies full pairwise
orthogonality of the orbit**, over any commutative ring. -/
theorem pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices {i : ι}
    (h : ∀ j ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i, i ≠ j → P.pairing i j = 0) :
    (P.orbitIndices σ i : Set ι).Pairwise P.IsOrthogonal := by
  -- Powers of `σ` act transitively on the cyclic orbit while preserving `P.pairing`.
  have hpair : ∀ j ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i, ∀ k ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i, j ≠ k → P.pairing j k = 0 := by
    intro j hj k hk hjk
    have hij : i ∈ P.orbitIndices σ j := by
      rw [orbitIndices_eq_of_mem hj]
      exact self_mem_orbitIndices P σ i
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := mem_orbitIndices_iff_exists_pow.mp hij
    have hmIdx : ∀ z, (σ ^ m).indexEquiv z = (σ.indexEquiv ^ m) z := fun z ↦
      congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe (map_pow (Equiv.indexHom P) σ m)) z
    have hl : (σ ^ m).indexEquiv k ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i := by
      rw [mem_orbitIndices, hmIdx]
      exact (mem_orbitIndices.mp hk).trans
        (Equiv.Perm.sameCycle_pow_right.mpr (Equiv.Perm.SameCycle.refl _ _))
    have hil : i ≠ (σ ^ m).indexEquiv k := by
      rw [← hm, ← hmIdx]
      exact (σ ^ m).indexEquiv.injective.ne hjk
    rw [← (σ ^ m).toHom.pairing (i := j) (j := k), hmIdx j, hm]
    exact h _ hl hil
  exact fun j hj k hk hjk ↦ ⟨hpair j hj k hk hjk, hpair k hk j hj hjk.symm⟩

/-- A `σ`-orbit of root indices is pairwise orthogonal if and only if its base root `i` has zero
pairing with every other root in the orbit. -/
theorem pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices_iff {i : ι} :
    (P.orbitIndices σ i : Set ι).Pairwise P.IsOrthogonal ↔
      ∀ j ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i, i ≠ j → P.pairing i j = 0 :=
  ⟨fun h _ hj hij ↦ (h (self_mem_orbitIndices P σ i) hj hij).1,
    pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices⟩

/-- **Any commuting product of reflections over a `σ`-orbit lies in `P.fixedWeylGroup σ`.** -/
theorem noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_mem_fixedWeylGroup (i : ι)
    (comm : (P.orbitIndices σ i : Set ι).Pairwise (Function.onFun Commute (weylGroup.ofIdx P))) :
    (P.orbitIndices σ i).noncommProd (weylGroup.ofIdx P) comm ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ := by
  rw [mem_fixedWeylGroup_iff_weylGroupEquiv, Equiv.weylGroupEquiv_noncommProd_ofIdx]
  exact Finset.noncommProd_congr
    ((map_orbitIndices σ (fun _ ↦ rfl) i).trans (orbitIndices_indexEquiv P σ i))
    (fun _ _ ↦ rfl) _

/-- All coroots in a single `σ`-orbit take the same value on any `σ`-fixed weight. -/
private lemma coroot'_eq_of_mem_orbitIndices_of_mem_fixedSubmodule {i j : ι}
    (hj : j ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i) {x : M} (hx : x ∈ LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) :
    P.coroot' j x = P.coroot' i x := by
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := mem_orbitIndices_iff_exists_pow.mp hj
  clear hj
  induction k with
  | zero => simp
  | succ k ih =>
    conv_lhs => rw [pow_succ', Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, ← LinearMap.mem_fixedSubmodule_iff.mp hx]
    rw [σ.toHom.coroot'_weightMap, ih]

/-- **Action of an orthogonal orbit reflection product on `σ`-fixed weights**: on `E^σ`, the
commuting product acts as `x ↦ x - ⟨x, αᵢ^∨⟩ • P.orbitSum σ i`. -/
theorem noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_smul_of_mem_fixedSubmodule {i : ι}
    (hs : (P.orbitIndices σ i : Set ι).Pairwise P.IsOrthogonal) {x : M}
    (hx : x ∈ LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap) :
    (P.orbitIndices σ i).noncommProd (weylGroup.ofIdx P)
      (weylGroup.pairwise_commute_ofIdx_of_isOrthogonal P hs) • x =
      x - P.coroot' i x • P.orbitSum σ i := by
  rw [weylGroup.noncommProd_ofIdx_smul P hs, orbitSum_def, Finset.smul_sum]
  congr 1
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j hj ↦ by
    rw [coroot'_eq_of_mem_orbitIndices_of_mem_fixedSubmodule hj hx]

end OrbitReflection

namespace Base

section Exhaustion

variable [Finite ι] [CharZero R] [IsDomain R] [P.IsCrystallographic] [P.IsReduced]

/-- Right multiplication of `w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ` by the reflection product over the `σ`-orbit
of a simple inversion `i` lowers the inversion count by `#(P.orbitIndices σ i)`. -/
theorem ncard_inversions_mul_noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx {b : P.Base} {σ : P.Aut}
    (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut) {w : P.weylGroup} (hw : w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ)
    {i : ι} (hi : i ∈ b.support) (hiw : i ∈ inversions P b w)
    (hs : (P.orbitIndices σ i : Set ι).Pairwise P.IsOrthogonal) :
    (inversions P b (w * (P.orbitIndices σ i).noncommProd (weylGroup.ofIdx P)
      (weylGroup.pairwise_commute_ofIdx_of_isOrthogonal P hs))).ncard +
      #(P.orbitIndices σ i) = (inversions P b w).ncard :=
  ncard_inversions_mul_noncommProd_ofIdx_of_subset P w b hs
    (b.orbitIndices_subset_support hσ hi) (b.orbitIndices_subset_inversions hσ hw hiw)

/-- **The fixed Weyl group of a based automorphism with orthogonal simple-root orbits is generated
by the simple-orbit reflection products** (the exhaustion half of Stembridge, Claim 3). No order on
the coefficient ring or spanning hypothesis is required. -/
theorem fixedWeylGroup_eq_closure (b : P.Base) {σ : P.Aut} (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut)
    (horth : ∀ i ∈ b.support, ∀ j ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i, i ≠ j → P.pairing i j = 0) :
    P.fixedWeylGroup σ = Subgroup.closure (range fun i : b.support ↦
      (P.orbitIndices σ (i : ι)).noncommProd (weylGroup.ofIdx P)
        (weylGroup.pairwise_commute_ofIdx_of_isOrthogonal P
          (pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices (horth i.1 i.2)))) := by
  set gen : b.support → P.weylGroup := fun i ↦
    (P.orbitIndices σ (i : ι)).noncommProd (weylGroup.ofIdx P)
      (weylGroup.pairwise_commute_ofIdx_of_isOrthogonal P
        (pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices (horth i.1 i.2)))
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ((Subgroup.closure_le _).mpr ?_)
  · -- Strong induction on the number of inversions of `w ∈ W^σ`.
    suffices ∀ n : ℕ, ∀ w : P.weylGroup, (inversions P b w).ncard = n →
        w ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ → w ∈ Subgroup.closure (range gen) from
      fun w hw ↦ this _ w rfl hw
    intro n
    induction n using Nat.strong_induction_on with
    | ind n ih =>
      intro w hcard hw
      by_cases hw1 : w = 1
      · exact hw1 ▸ one_mem _
      · obtain ⟨i, hi, hiw⟩ := exists_mem_support_mem_inversions_of_ne_one P b hw1
        have hgen_fixed : gen ⟨i, hi⟩ ∈ P.fixedWeylGroup σ :=
          noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_mem_fixedWeylGroup i _
        have hgen_cl : gen ⟨i, hi⟩ ∈ Subgroup.closure (range gen) :=
          Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨⟨i, hi⟩, rfl⟩
        have hdrop : (inversions P b (w * gen ⟨i, hi⟩)).ncard +
            #(P.orbitIndices σ i) = n :=
          (ncard_inversions_mul_noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx hσ hw hi hiw
            (pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices (horth i hi))).trans hcard
        have hpos : 0 < #(P.orbitIndices σ i) := card_orbitIndices_pos P σ i
        have hlt : (inversions P b (w * gen ⟨i, hi⟩)).ncard < n := by omega
        have hw' : w * gen ⟨i, hi⟩ ∈ Subgroup.closure (range gen) :=
          ih _ hlt (w * gen ⟨i, hi⟩) rfl (mul_mem hw hgen_fixed)
        have hmul : (w * gen ⟨i, hi⟩) * gen ⟨i, hi⟩ = w := by
          rw [mul_assoc, weylGroup.noncommProd_ofIdx_mul_self, mul_one]
        exact hmul ▸ mul_mem hw' hgen_cl
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_mem_fixedWeylGroup i.1 _

/-- Inside the group `P.fixedWeylGroup σ` itself, the simple-orbit reflection products generate the
whole group `⊤`. -/
theorem top_eq_closure_fixedWeylGroup (b : P.Base) {σ : P.Aut} (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut)
    (horth : ∀ i ∈ b.support, ∀ j ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i, i ≠ j → P.pairing i j = 0) :
    (⊤ : Subgroup (P.fixedWeylGroup σ)) = Subgroup.closure (range fun i : b.support ↦
      (⟨(P.orbitIndices σ (i : ι)).noncommProd (weylGroup.ofIdx P)
          (weylGroup.pairwise_commute_ofIdx_of_isOrthogonal P
            (pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices (horth i.1 i.2))),
        noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_mem_fixedWeylGroup i.1 _⟩ : P.fixedWeylGroup σ)) := by
  set genFixed : b.support → P.fixedWeylGroup σ := fun i ↦
    ⟨(P.orbitIndices σ (i : ι)).noncommProd (weylGroup.ofIdx P)
        (weylGroup.pairwise_commute_ofIdx_of_isOrthogonal P
          (pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices (horth i.1 i.2))),
      noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_mem_fixedWeylGroup i.1 _⟩
  have hmap : (Subgroup.closure (range genFixed)).map (P.fixedWeylGroup σ).subtype =
      P.fixedWeylGroup σ := by
    rw [MonoidHom.map_closure, ← range_comp]
    exact (b.fixedWeylGroup_eq_closure hσ horth).symm
  symm
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  rintro u -
  have hu : (u : P.weylGroup) ∈
      (Subgroup.closure (range genFixed)).map (P.fixedWeylGroup σ).subtype := by
    rw [hmap]
    exact u.2
  rcases Subgroup.mem_map.mp hu with ⟨v, hv, hvu⟩
  rwa [← Subtype.ext hvu]

/-- **Image of `W^σ` in `GL(E^σ)`**: together with
`RootPairing.Base.toModuleAut_fixedWeylGroup_injective` and
`RootPairing.noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_smul_of_mem_fixedSubmodule`, this identifies `W^σ`
isomorphically with the subgroup of `E^σ ≃ₗ[R] E^σ` generated by the restricted simple-orbit
reflections (Stembridge, Claim 3). -/
theorem range_toModuleAut_fixedWeylGroup (b : P.Base) {σ : P.Aut} (hσ : σ ∈ b.basedAut)
    (horth : ∀ i ∈ b.support, ∀ j ∈ P.orbitIndices σ i, i ≠ j → P.pairing i j = 0) :
    (DistribMulAction.toModuleAut R (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap)
      (S := P.fixedWeylGroup σ)).range =
      Subgroup.closure (range fun i : b.support ↦
        DistribMulAction.toLinearEquiv R (LinearMap.fixedSubmodule σ.weightMap)
          (⟨(P.orbitIndices σ (i : ι)).noncommProd (weylGroup.ofIdx P)
              (weylGroup.pairwise_commute_ofIdx_of_isOrthogonal P
                (pairwise_isOrthogonal_orbitIndices (horth i.1 i.2))),
            noncommProd_orbitIndices_ofIdx_mem_fixedWeylGroup i.1 _⟩ : P.fixedWeylGroup σ)) := by
  rw [MonoidHom.range_eq_map, b.top_eq_closure_fixedWeylGroup hσ horth, MonoidHom.map_closure,
    ← range_comp]
  rfl

end Exhaustion

end Base

end RootPairing
